{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527385-v5-homebrew-trujah-loresheet","id":1527385,"title":"(V5 Homebrew) Trujah Loresheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-24T10:21:40-08:00","id":1527385,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5 Homebrew) Trujah Loresheet","content":"Because I'm bored as hell, I thought I'd do this one too. Lemme know what you all think. Commentary in italics.<br /> <br /> <b>The Elois (bloodline loresheet, Brujah only)</b><br /> <br /> Obligatory shitpost fluff part. We should all know the score by now: these assholes claim they're descended from Ilyes, not Troile, and have <i>just </i>a little bit of a grudge over the whole &quot;Carthage&quot; thing, just in the opposite way of other Brujah. Just...forget the whole TMR crap for now. Anyhow, onto the part that really matters!<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Insidious Beast</b>: The Elois' retain the unusually powerful and insurgent Beasts of their clan, but yours is not merely a creature of base instinct. Rather, it acts strategically with its long-term goal of permanent control ever in mind, sacrificing nightly battles for control to push you to justify your existence, rationalize your actions, and question your morality. Your difficulties to resist fury frenzy are reduced by one (to a minimum of one), but you take the Lasombra alternate bane Callousness instead of your usual clan bane.<br /> <br /> <i>(Callousness is more or less a pitch-perfect translation of the OG Trujah clan flaw, no need to reinvent the wheel here. But given this is a one-dot merit and Callousness is a particularly nasty bane, it needs something to provide net benefit and balance things out. -1 difficulty translates to two extra dice, which is fair enough...for a newb trap that disincentivizes riding the wave. The most common reason to ride the wave -- which doesn't require a roll in v5 -- is to avoid collateral damage and Stains, and a smart Beast wouldn't want that, now would it.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Atropos' Hand</b>: The Elois exploit Celerity to not just alter perception of time but also to externalize the supernatural stasis that preserves their undead forms, referring to their quasi-discipline as Temporis. At this level, you have gained the ability to reverse the last few seconds' of time for yourself, changing catastrophic consequences of your actions for the better. Once per story, when you roll a messy critical or bestial failure, you may make a Rouse Check and convert that result into a critical win or failure respectively. However, you retain your memory of the consequences averted, and as a result gain one or more Stains (your ST will decide).<br /> <br /> <i>(We all knew Temporis was gonna show up here. It's the Trujah's coolest &quot;hat&quot; after all. Luckily, v5 Celerity is basically already Temporis, and all that needs to happen is adding that dash of utility to bring out that Temporis flavor. Negating a single messy critical or bestial failure once per story is admittedly powerful for a two-dot merit, but it has strong negative synergy with the one-dot merit. If you have Callousness, the last thing you want is Stains as that Remorse check can and will bite your undead ass.<br /> <br /> That's pretty much the theme: the merits are powerful, but the cost is being hit where the character is weakest and all but forcing fast degeneration for excessive use. Past editions cost excessive blood, health levels, or Willpower, but I see mucking around with time itself as an act of incredible hubris that well should quickly separate a vampire from their humanity.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Fair is Foul</b>: The Elois have never forgotten -- or forgiven -- Troile's diablerie of the true Brujah antediluvian, and punish Troile's descendants at every opportunity. Any time the harm or destruction of another Brujah is your Desire, add two dice to any roll that immediately furthers that Desire. In addition, if you accomplish that Desire, you may convert a single aggravated Willpower damage to superficial, instead of healing a superficial Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> <i>(This one pretty much speaks for itself. Trujah says &quot;fuck that guy in particular&quot;, and if that guy in particular is the target of their bloodline-wide vendetta, Trujah gets bonuses for fucking that guy in particular. There's no way I didn't make the name of this one a callback to the Gehenna scenario.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Clotho's Gift</b>: Your advanced understanding of Temporis has granted you the ability to slow your perception of time, allowing you to carefully consider your options at points others must simply react or act on intuition. If you do not already have the Celerity power of Fleetness, take it at no cost -- you do not necessarily have the discipline power, but rather a special variant of your own. This power works like Fleetness, except you add your Celerity rating to non-combat Wits and Composure tests. If you do have (or later acquire) Fleetness, when you use the power you may make a second Rouse Check to substitute your Wits or Composure rating (whichever is higher) for Dexterity in addition to Fleetness' usual effect.<br /> <br /> <i>(This one's pretty self-explanatory, too. Mechanically, it's somewhere between OG Prediction and Insight, applying Celerity to mental or social tasks instead of physical, and applying mental/social traits to physical tasks. Just, without the overly ridiculous dice pool and action economy shenanigans of OG elder disciplines.<br /> <br /> I guess it's time to address the elephant in the room, which is why I'm switching around the names of the powers. Clotho, Lachesis, and Atropos weren't just the spinner, measurer, and cutter of the thread of life; Atropos was commonly associated with the past, Clotho the present, and Lachesis the future. The two-dot merit alters the immediate past, the four-dot merit influences the present, and the five-dot merit shapes the future, so switching up the names just seems more thematically appropriate.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Lachesis' Kiss</b>: You have -- or at least believe you have -- mastered Temporis, and can perceive the multitude of potential timelines that branch from the present, based on the immediate consequences of your choices. As such, you have limited ability to ensure the timeline which does occur, is that most beneficial to you in the moment. When willing a Blood Surge, you may substitute your Celerity rating as bonus dice instead of those determined by your Blood Potency. However, if you do and fail your Rouse Check, you gain a Stain in addition to the Hunger as visions of the harm you have yet to cause flood your mind.<br /> <br /> <i>(This is basically just a straightforward adaptation of Insight/Cheat the Fates, but adapted to v5 mechanics. Again there's not much to say here, save that using it as a replacement to default blood surge mechanics will help curtail dice pool shenanigans.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T18:52:52-08:00","id":1527406,"title":"","content":"Nice work!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T09:08:56-08:00","id":1527428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527385-v5-homebrew-trujah-loresheet?p=1527406#post1527406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice work!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> I was split between homebrewing additional Celerity powers to represent Temporis, or make it loresheet-specific powers and power substitutes. V5 Celerity is written decently and broadly enough to make justifying an entire discipline sub-tree (a la Vicissitude) incredibly hard, and most Celerity powers are so good &quot;Temporis&quot; variants would have to be incredibly strong to incentivize taking. The only one that's really &quot;discipline power&quot; powerful in its own right is Clotho's Gift, and that's because it's just Fleetness reskinned to boost Wits/Composure instead of Dexterity.<br /> <br /> So, better to split the difference and just make Temporis part of the loresheet. Still, I might write up Internal Recursion as a Celerity/Presence amalgam, and Lapse as a Celerity/Potence amalgam.<br /> <br /> But, reading it again, I realized my write-up for Clotho's Gift is a little confusing...<i>[EDIT: I realized after hitting &quot;post&quot;, no it isn't and additional clarifying language isn't actually necessary.]</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 12-25-2023, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T12:18:56-08:00","id":1527570,"title":"","content":"Certainly a better take on the bloodline then what I have read in the official lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T17:56:13-08:00","id":1527616,"title":"","content":"Hoping there is no objection to using this thread to talk about other True Brujah matters. The True Brujah was one of those concepts I originally did not like, but they've grown on me over the years. I'm not opposed to the substance of the bloodline - that they are the surviving lineage of the actual founder after being massacred by the followers of Troile - but Temporis as a Discipline irritated me. And for a long time I did not appreciate the sourcebook Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand. Now I'm much more willing to consider using them in chronicles, but first I need to work out details so I understand how I can use them.<br /> <br /> First, how many should there be in total? DSotBH tells us that the Tal'mahe'Ra has less than 200 members. We have 14-15 bloodlines in them (if we count clan and anti-tribu separately). So each bloodline has an average of around 12-14 members. I am going to arbitrarily select that average as the number of True Brujah within the Hand likely divided between members hiding in the Camarilla and the Eastern Hand. (I find it extremely unlikely any would be members of the Sabbat).<br /> <br /> We also know not all True Brujah are members of the Hand. We know some are Inconnu and others could be Autarkis. Some could be in other small Jyhad level groups like the Children of Osiris. Possibly some might still be members of the Camarilla (though not as infiltrators for the True Hand) under hidden identities. I'll arbitrarily say collectively this group equals the numbers of those inside the Hand. So we only have between 20-30 True Brujah in the entire world as originally depicted.<br /> <br /> Second, how individually powerful and old are they? Since character creation rules in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand start at the 10<sup>th</sup> Generation, not 13<sup>th</sup>, I will assume all members of the True Brujah are 10<sup>th</sup> generation or earlier. The character creation system there therefore allows you to create a 5th generation True Brujah, which means the bloodline's &quot;founder&quot; was 4th generation a thus a childe of Ilyes. Personally I dislike the presence of someone who actually knew the antedeluvians personally so I'd limit the original survivor of Troile's massacre to be a member of the 5th generation (you could feel differently). All True Brujah are descended from this survivor. Of course given the age of this vampire, he's likely in torpor as possibly any of his 6th generation children.<br /> <br /> The bloodline does not seem to have a single ruler (they seem very collegial towards each other) so I think the senior leadership of the True Brujah are probably a group of elder 7<sup>th</sup> generation True Brujah still active who get along well and tell stories about \u201cgrandpa\u201d. The remaining 8<sup>th</sup>, 9<sup>th</sup>, and 10<sup>th</sup> generation True Brujah are all descended from them. A four level pyramid can provide us something like three members of the 7<sup>th</sup>, then five of the 8<sup>th</sup>, seven of the 9<sup>th</sup>, and nine of the 10<sup>th</sup>. That is twenty four members that is close enough to our target of twenty to thirty. These aren\u2019t exact numbers for each generation, but probably close enough.<br /> <br /> This post is getting long so I'll cut it now and continue this later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T17:57:59-08:00","id":1527617,"title":"","content":"Once again simply editing a post gets marked as spam and suddenly requires approval. I need to remember to just let things rot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}